4. LinuxCNC
   License:   LGPL v3 / GPL v2 (mixed)
   Source:    https://github.com/LinuxCNC/linuxcnc
   Website:   https://linuxcnc.org

   This project uses LinuxCNC's Python bindings and runs as a
   companion application alongside LinuxCNC. It is not a derivative
   of LinuxCNC itself.

   Additionally bundled from the LinuxCNC source tree:
   - scripts/kins_oracle/trtfuncs.c and kins_util.c (v2.9.4, GPL v2) —
     vendored VERBATIM as the compiled test oracle for the viewer's
     xyzac/xyzbc-trt kinematics mirrors (see scripts/kins_oracle/README.md)
   - examples/sim_config/machine-xyzac/ STL geometry — generated by
     scripts/vismach_to_stl.py from LinuxCNC's vismach xyzac-trt-gui
     sample (GPL v2+, Rudy du Preez)
   - examples/sim_config/remap_subs/ — adapted from the LinuxCNC 2.9.4
     table-rotary-tilting sample config's switchkins remaps (GPL v2+)
   - scripts/kins_oracle/xyzacb_trsrn.comp (LinuxCNC master, GPL v2,
     David Mueller) — vendored VERBATIM as the compiled test oracle for
     the TWP machine's switchable kinematics (identity/TCP/TOOL-plane;
     see scripts/kins_oracle/README.md). Uses master's handle-style HAL
     pin API, so it is compiled against stubs by the harness and CANNOT
     be halcompile'd on 2.9.
   - examples/sim_config/twp/xyzacb_trsrn.comp (master @493926b56c, GPL
     v2, David Mueller) — vendored VERBATIM as the INSTALLABLE runtime
     module for the TWP sim config; this pre-2.10 revision uses the
     classic pointer HAL API that LinuxCNC 2.9's halcompile accepts. Its
     kinematics math is character-identical to the oracle copy above, and
     test_kins_oracle_parity.py fails if they ever diverge.
   - examples/sim_config/twp/ (master @493926b56c, GPL v2, David
     Mueller) — the Tilted Work Plane remap stack
     (configs/sim/axis/vismach/5axis/twp/): python/util.py, toplevel.py
     and twp-helper-comp.py verbatim; python/remap.py FORKED (GPL v2,
     edits tagged LCNC-SUITE) so the preview interpreter runs the plane
     math and emits webui marker comments; remap_subs/*.ngc wrappers
     carry added (WEBUI_KINSTYPE=n) markers; demos/simple_example.ngc and
     demos/square.ngc are vendored VERBATIM from the same config's
     demos/. See its README.md.
   - examples/sim_config/machine-xyzacb-trsrn/ STL geometry — generated
     by scripts/vismach_to_stl_trsrn.py, whose machine layout, kinematic
     constants and frame placement are taken from LinuxCNC's vismach
     xyzacb-trsrn-gui sample (master @493926b56c, GPL v2, David Mueller).
     The meshes are NOT copies: the assembly is re-derived from the kins
     pins so it is mechanically coherent at the shipped pivot values.


